{"1-10":{"people":[{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":5,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"saul-h7586g","name":"Saul","kind":"person","brief":"King of Israel,","count":5,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":3},{"id":"jonathan-h3083h","name":"Jonathan","kind":"person","brief":"David's friend","count":2,"firstVerse":4}],"places":[{"id":"amalek-h6002g","name":"Amalek","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":2,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"ziklag-h6860","name":"Ziklag","kind":"place","brief":"In Philistia","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"gilboa-mount-h1533h","name":"Gilboa Mount","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":6}],"words":[{"base":"H7586","lemma":"שָׁאוּל","tr":"sha·ul","gloss":"Saul","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":406},{"base":"H1732","lemma":"דָּוִד","tr":"da·vid","gloss":"David","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":1075},{"base":"H4191","lemma":"מוּת","tr":"mut","gloss":"to die","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":840},{"base":"H5046","lemma":"נָגַד","tr":"na·gad","gloss":"to tell","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":370},{"base":"H5307","lemma":"נָפַל","tr":"na·phal","gloss":"to fall: fall","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":434},{"base":"H0310","lemma":"אַחַר","tr":"a·char","gloss":"after","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":715},{"base":"H3083","lemma":"יְהוֹנָתָן","tr":"ye·ho·na·tan","gloss":"Jonathan","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":82},{"base":"H2009","lemma":"הִנֵּה","tr":"hin·neh","gloss":"behold","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":843},{"base":"H9030","lemma":"נִי","tr":"ni","gloss":"me","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":908},{"base":"H4480","lemma":"מִן־","tr":"min","gloss":"from","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1187}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1SA","chapter":4,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"“I have just come from the battle,” the man said to Eli. “I fled from there today.” “What happened, my son?” Eli asked.","from":4},{"book":"1SA","chapter":31,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"Now the Philistines fought against Israel, and the men of Israel fled before them, and many fell slain on Mount Gilboa.","from":4},{"book":"1SA","chapter":31,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"So Saul, his three sons, his armor-bearer, and all his men died together that same day.","from":4},{"book":"1CH","chapter":10,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"Now the Philistines fought against Israel, and the men of Israel fled before them, and many fell slain on Mount Gilboa.","from":4},{"book":"1CH","chapter":10,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"So Saul died together with his three sons and all his house.","from":4},{"book":"1SA","chapter":4,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"That same day a Benjamite ran from the battle line all the way to Shiloh, with his clothes torn and dirt on his head.","from":2},{"book":"JDG","chapter":9,"verse":54,"verseEnd":54,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"He quickly called his armor-bearer, saying, “Draw your sword and kill me, lest they say of me, ‘A woman killed him.’” So Abimelechʼs armor-bearer ran his sword through him, and he died.","from":10},{"book":"MAT","chapter":7,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"For with the same judgment you pronounce, you will be judged; and with the measure you use, it will be measured to you.","from":10}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":3}]},"11-16":{"people":[{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":5,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"jonathan-h3083h","name":"Jonathan","kind":"person","brief":"David's friend","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"saul-h7586g","name":"Saul","kind":"person","brief":"King of Israel,","count":1,"firstVerse":12}],"places":[{"id":"amalek-h6002g","name":"Amalek","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":1,"firstVerse":13}],"words":[{"base":"H1732","lemma":"דָּוִד","tr":"da·vid","gloss":"David","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":1075},{"base":"H4899","lemma":"מָשִׁיחַ","tr":"ma·shi·ach","gloss":"anointed","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":39},{"base":"H5288","lemma":"נַ֫עַר","tr":"na·ar","gloss":"youth","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":239},{"base":"H0595","lemma":"אָֽנֹכִ֫י","tr":"a·no·khi","gloss":"I","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":359},{"base":"H4191","lemma":"מוּת","tr":"mut","gloss":"to die","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":840},{"base":"H6003","lemma":"עֲמָלֵקִי","tr":"a·ma·le·qi","gloss":"Amalekite","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":12},{"base":"H6684","lemma":"צוּם","tr":"tsum","gloss":"to fast","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":21},{"base":"H5594","lemma":"סָפַד","tr":"sa·phad","gloss":"to mourn","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":30},{"base":"H0335","lemma":"אַי","tr":"ay","gloss":"where?","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":39},{"base":"H6293","lemma":"פָּגַע","tr":"pa·ga","gloss":"to fall on","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":46}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1SA","chapter":26,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"But David said to Abishai, “Do not destroy him, for who can extend a hand against the Lordʼs anointed and be guiltless?”","from":14},{"book":"MAT","chapter":27,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"All the people answered, “His blood be on us and on our children!”","from":16},{"book":"NUM","chapter":12,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"I speak with him face to face, clearly and not in riddles; he sees the form of the LORD. Why then were you unafraid to speak against My servant Moses?”","from":14},{"book":"1SA","chapter":24,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"So he said to his men, “The LORD forbid that I should do such a thing to my master, the LORDʼs anointed. May I never lift my hand against him, since he is the LORDʼs anointed.”","from":14},{"book":"1SA","chapter":31,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Then Saul said to his armor-bearer, “Draw your sword and run me through with it, or these uncircumcised men will come and run me through and torture me!” But his armor-bearer was terrified and refused to do it. So Saul took his own sword and fell on it.","from":14},{"book":"2SA","chapter":13,"verse":31,"verseEnd":31,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Then the king stood up, tore his clothes, and lay down on the ground. And all his servants stood by with their clothes torn.","from":11},{"book":"PSA","chapter":105,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"“Do not touch My anointed ones! Do no harm to My prophets!”","from":14},{"book":"LUK","chapter":19,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"His master replied, ‘You wicked servant, I will judge you by your own words. So you knew that I am a harsh man, withdrawing what I did not deposit and reaping what I did not sow?","from":16}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":3}]},"17-27":{"people":[{"id":"jonathan-h3083h","name":"Jonathan","kind":"person","brief":"David's friend","count":5,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"saul-h7586g","name":"Saul","kind":"person","brief":"King of Israel,","count":5,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"jashar-h3477h","name":"Jashar","kind":"person","brief":"Author of book","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":2,"firstVerse":19}],"places":[{"id":"ashkelon-h0831","name":"Ashkelon","kind":"place","brief":"In Philistia","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"gath-h1661","name":"Gath","kind":"place","brief":"In Philistia","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"philistia-h6429","name":"Philistia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"gilboa-h1533g","name":"Gilboa","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":21}],"words":[{"base":"H3083","lemma":"יְהוֹנָתָן","tr":"ye·ho·na·tan","gloss":"Jonathan","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":82},{"base":"H1368","lemma":"גִּבּוֹר","tr":"gib·bor","gloss":"mighty man","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":159},{"base":"H7586","lemma":"שָׁאוּל","tr":"sha·ul","gloss":"Saul","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":406},{"base":"H0349","lemma":"אֵיךְ","tr":"ekh","gloss":"how?","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":82},{"base":"H2491","lemma":"חָלָל","tr":"cha·lal","gloss":"slain: killed","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":94},{"base":"H0408","lemma":"אַל","tr":"al","gloss":"not","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":724},{"base":"H5307","lemma":"נָפַל","tr":"na·phal","gloss":"to fall: fall","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":434},{"base":"H0160","lemma":"אַהֲבָה","tr":"a·ha·vah","gloss":"love","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":38},{"base":"H1323","lemma":"בַּת","tr":"bat","gloss":"daughter","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":588},{"base":"H4043","lemma":"מָגֵן","tr":"ma·gen","gloss":"shield","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":63}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1SA","chapter":20,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"And Jonathan had David reaffirm his vow out of love for him, for Jonathan loved David as he loved himself.","from":26},{"book":"JER","chapter":4,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Behold, he advances like the clouds, his chariots like the whirlwind. His horses are swifter than eagles. Woe to us, for we are ruined!","from":23},{"book":"DEU","chapter":4,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"For what nation is great enough to have a god as near to them as the LORD our God is to us whenever we call on Him?","from":19},{"book":"DEU","chapter":4,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"And what nation is great enough to have righteous statutes and ordinances like this entire law I set before you today?","from":19},{"book":"JOS","chapter":10,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"So the sun stood still and the moon stopped until the nation took vengeance upon its enemies. Is this not written in the Book of Jashar? “So the sun stopped in the middle of the sky and delayed going down about a full day.”","from":18},{"book":"1SA","chapter":18,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"After David had finished speaking with Saul, the souls of Jonathan and David were knit together, and Jonathan loved him as himself.","from":26},{"book":"1SA","chapter":18,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"And Jonathan removed the robe he was wearing and gave it to David, along with his tunic, his sword, his bow, and his belt.","from":22},{"book":"1SA","chapter":18,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"And Jonathan removed the robe he was wearing and gave it to David, along with his tunic, his sword, his bow, and his belt.","from":26}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":3},{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2},{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]}}